## Stage92 24H32 TX completion handoff — 20261106
- Branch: work/stage91-tx-submission-callback-v1
- Source baseline: 5a1fe872661def012aedd1d721cfae25b8ed1851
- Result: IMPLEMENTED_SOURCE_ONLY_VALIDATION_PENDING
- Target ABI: 24H32 TX completion action uses UInt32 packet-count return; callback returns zero (no callback packets).
- Handoff: deferred controller-workloop worker uses public IOSkywalkTxCompletionQueue::enqueuePackets(const IOSkywalkPacket **, UInt32, IOOptionBits) synchronously; success means the queue ran completePackets and the target packet/buffer completion chain before adapter packet retain is released.
- Retry: enqueue preflight failure leaves ticket/packet/adapter retains intact and returns ticket to Completed for timer retry.
- Teardown: worker remains alive while tickets exist or backend-completion callbacks remain in flight; radio stop + PCI/DMA fence precede adapter unbind; worker removal and notifier clear follow empty-ticket plus zero-callback proof; queue owner/pools released afterward.
- Caveat: Skywalk completion API has no verified per-packet Tx-success flag; RTW88 transmitted result is not encoded into undocumented option bits. Separate telemetry remains open.
- Report: Development/Logs/stage92-tx-completion-handoff-24H32-20261106.md
- Required target-Mac validation: 11 host/source tests plus eight compile-only objects; no link/sign/install/load/hardware test.
- Queue registration, queue enable, native interface publication, radio start and OpenCore/SIP/NVRAM changes remain fenced.

